stimuli.content:
In a certain code:
'P α Q' means 'P is 6 m to the east of Q';
'P β Q' means 'P is 8 m to the north of Q';
'P γ Q' means 'P is 6 m to the west of Q';
'P δ Q' means 'P is 8 m to the south of Q'.

The following are true: K α L, M β K, N γ M, O δ L, T γ O.

questions.question_text:
In a certain code:
'A ◇ B' means 'A is the father of B';
'A ○ B' means 'A is the daughter of B';
'A △ B' means 'A is the brother of B';
'A ▽ B' means 'A is the wife of B'.

If 'K ▽ L △ M ○ N', how is K related to N?
